DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't try to catch the falling AI names.</b> Intel, Alphabet and the chip stocks are being repriced on spending and cash-flow worries; keep regular investing (DCA) in broad funds instead of loading up on one fallen name.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> Health care and consumer staples held up this week; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on AI.",
"<b>Rates are still high.</b> Hot inflation and $104 oil keep a December hike likely (about 71-75%); avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can.",
"<b>Cash and short-term bonds still pay.</b> They are a calm place to park money while the AI trade settles.",
"<b>Budget for higher fuel.</b> Oil rose 15% in October and Iran strike risk around the 3 Nov midterms is real; diesel is about $6.32 in the US.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It fell to a one-year low near $3,887; if you hold some, keep it a small slice and don't chase either way.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> The $6.3B Binance hack shows exchange risk; don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: be patient and selective.</b> The SET fell to 1,518.59, close to the 1,500 support, but foreigners turned buyers (฿1.06B). In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 26.2 = Fear, near the Extreme Fear line, down from 34.6 after Friday's tech selloff (it was 16.7 a week ago). Momentum and safe-haven demand are in extreme fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated, about unchanged: more Hormuz ship attacks raised spillover risk, but Qatari mediation, a possible Putin-Zelensky call and Trump saying the war will 'end soon' offset it."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 14.6 = extreme fear: Friday's 1.8% drop pushed the index below its 100-day average."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 32.4 = fear (92 NYSE highs vs 169 lows Friday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 37.2 = fear: Friday's selling spread beyond big tech."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 27.8 = lots of protection buying, a fearful sign."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 26.5 = fear: the VIX jumped to about 19.4 from 17.2."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 2.2 = extreme fear: bonds have beaten stocks as money hid from tech."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 43.0 = fear, slipping from neutral: lenders are getting a bit more careful."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 66 (unchanged): possible US strikes on Iran after the midterms are offset by Qatari mediation and Trump saying the war will end soon. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 38 (down from 39), the biggest weight: Russian strikes blacked out Dnipro, but Putin says he's open to a call with Zelensky."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 74 (up from 72): Iran says four tankers hit mines in Hormuz, October had a record number of ship attacks, and the Houthis fired at Aden and toward Riyadh."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 22 (down from 24): Qatari mediators are in Tehran, and G20 ministers including Lavrov met in Atlanta."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats; Trump said any deal needs a guarantee Iran never gets a nuclear weapon."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,580 Friday (−1.82%), its worst day since June and below its 100-day average."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −1.09% Friday."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −2.86% Friday as Intel crashed 29% and chips sold off; the Nasdaq 100 briefly hit correction territory."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.93% Friday: below 5% as investors bought bonds for safety."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$104.1 settle Friday (+2.1%), the highest since late April, on Iran strike fears."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$113.4 for the January contract (+2.4%); the expiring December contract hit $118."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.32/gal (AAA, 31 Oct), just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,887 = a one-year low after a 3.3% drop Friday, as higher oil kept Fed hike bets alive and investors sold gold to cover tech losses; $4,000 is now resistance."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$77.2k = bearish: a $6.3B Binance hack and the tech selloff pushed it to its lowest since mid-September."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 71-75% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec, as oil keeps inflation worries alive."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. About 102.0 Friday, little changed."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~157.5 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% on Friday but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT sees 2026 inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. SET 1,518.59 (−1.68% Fri 30 Oct), dragged by DELTA (−8.1%); 1,500-1,510 is the next support."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿1.06B on 30 Oct, ending two days of selling; October about −฿6.6B and year to date about +฿18.5B (our sums of SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
